    ],
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "section",
        "heading": "One shape, three places",
        "minutes": 3,
        "cells": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Press a chord box below to hear the chord. A power chord has two notes, a root and its 5th, with the root often played again on top. The three boxes show the same shape of the fingers, moved to other strings or another fret.\nStrum only the strings with dots, and rest the side of your picking hand on the other strings to keep them quiet.\nPractice until each chord sounds clean, with no other string ringing."
          },
          {
            "type": "tool",
            "tool": {
